        "original_id": "f152f4e1-ecfb-5282-bf01-6b175cbe4d2a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Muehlenbeckia, Euptelea\n- Animal species: Peristoreus viridipennis\n- Taxonomy: Eupteleaceae\n- Places: Southern Hemisphere, South America, Papua New Guinea, Australia, New Zealand, temperate locales north of the equator\n\nFacts:\n- Muehlenbeckia, also called the maidenhair genus, is native to the Southern Hemisphere, especially South America, Papua New Guinea, Australia, and New Zealand.\n- Muehlenbeckia has been introduced to temperate locales north of the equator by birds and by cultivation.\n- Euptelea is a genus of two species of flowering plants.\n- Euptelea is the only genus in the family Eupteleaceae.\n- Peristoreus viridipennis is associated with plants of the genus Muehlenbeckia.",
